templates/settings/settings.base.json:628:  "_model_pin_comment": "PLAN-163 T1.1 contingency (ADR-181 §Contingency) — session-default pin. CC 2.1.220 honors the top-level settings key \"model\" (zod: E.string().optional(); describe \"Override the default model used by Claude Code\"; source at 2.1.220 binary offset 226819212, sha256 8addc857..., between \"permissions\" and \"fallbackModel\"). Pinned to claude-opus-5-5 since ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357; Claude Opus 5.5 needs Claude Code >= 2.1.280). ADR-181 first pinned claude-opus-5 so that adding claude-sonnet-5 to availableModels could not silently flip the session default to the 2.1.220 sonnet-5 tier-default (enforceAvailableModels stops redirecting once sonnet-5 is allowed); claude-opus-5 stays the fallbackModel. ADOPTER NOTE: a fresh install therefore inherits claude-opus-5-5 as the session default (Opus 5.5 pricing $4/$20 per MTok). If that is not desired for your workload, override the value here (e.g. \"claude-sonnet-5\" or your tier default) or set env ANTHROPIC_MODEL / pass CLI --model per-session; the pinned value must be one that availableModels below admits: Claude Code replaces a pin the allowlist does not admit with the default model at startup (with a warning), and admits an id that extends an allowed entry by a - segment. scripts/upgrade.sh is stricter: it writes a new framework pin into an existing install only when that pin is an EXACT entry of its availableModels, and warns otherwise. Keep this key mirrored with .claude/settings.json in the framework repo (SessionDefaultPinTest).",
